    {
      "id": "t06-cumulative-ack-retires-canonical-gbn-descriptors",
      "introduced_by": "T06",
      "cause": "A cumulative ACK retires acknowledged descriptors from the canonical GBN map and clears a selected cursor that no longer names outstanding data.",
      "impact": "Three already-acknowledged retransmission attempts are omitted and completion advances by 251 ns. Task goodput increases from 73.2909 to 73.938 Gbps; affected port byte-throughput decreases because it no longer counts the three redundant attempts. Packet UIDs and downstream trace times change transitively while topology, inputs, unaffected ports, and unaffected nodes remain byte-identical.",
